{"id": 3094, "name": "Eveland Access Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.mahaskaconservation.com/cabins/eveland_access_campgrounds/", "lines": [" in April (weather permitting) and close the last full weekend in October. | | Can I reserve a campsite? | NO RESERVATIONS. Campsites are rented on a first come first serve basis. | | What is the cost to camp? | Cost is $20.00 dollars per night. Payment envelopes can be found at the kiosks situated on both sides of the campgrounds. Self registration is required. Fill out the payment envelope completely, enclose your ", " | MCCB follows state regulations. Campers may stay 14 consecutive nights. After the 14 consecutive nights, you must vacate the park for 24 hours. | | Does MCCB offer any camping incentives? | MCCB has coupon books. For $200.00 you get 11 coupons; pay for 10 nights and the 11th night is free. | | Does MCCB have water hook-ups? | NO. MCCB does have hydrants where you may fill tanks; however, campers are not allowed to"]}, {"url": "https://www.mahaskaconservation.com/", "lines": ["ouse | 4-5:30 pm Trick-or-Treating from campsite to campsite | (SUPPER BREAK) | 7-9 pm Lights & Sights Auto Campsite Tour through campground to vote for favorite decorated campsite. Line begins next to shelter house and $5 suggested/free-will donations are appreciated for campground improvements. Candy is given away at the end of the auto tour! | BARK Ranger Costume Parade (at Halloween Bash) | October 24, 2026 | Eve", " dog treats as we walk the route! At the shelter house, your dog can have fun bobbing for hotdogs and getting their paws stamped on a special BARK Ranger certificate. | BARK Ranger dog tags will be available to purchase $10 each. No registration is needed - just show up at the event! All dogs must be on a leash. | Halloween Lights & Sights Auto Tour (at Halloween Bash) | October 24, 2026 | Eveland Access Campground |", "campsite. | Pick up a ballot at the start of the route near the shelt